1:1-1 (* EXPECT-ERROR: is bound from the value parameter root *)
2:1-13 (* This was observed 2026-10-04 building exported variables, and\n   understood 2026-10-10.  The checker's CheckFile took the file's root\n   BY VALUE and bound u to each unit (`IF root.kids[i] IS SOME u').  It\n   handed u to a walk taking `VAR n: PTR Node', which rewrote a name\n   with `NEW (n, CHAR, ...)' in n's pool, the hidden one a VAR pointer\n   brings.  A binder's pool is its origin's, and the origin was a value\n   parameter's component, whose pool nobody named.  The generator fell\n   back to the calling frame, and the name was freed when CheckFile\n   returned.  The compiler read `unknown name: const voi' where a name\n   had been.  The checker refused a value parameter's component as such\n   a root, but not a binder on one.  It does now; the walk's holder\n   takes the root VAR, so the pool comes with it. *)
comments=2
